# Line endings are functional here, not cosmetic.
#
# start.sh is the macOS/Linux launcher: committed with CRLF it dies at the
# shebang ("bad interpreter: No such file or directory"), and shellcheck in
# CI would not catch it. START.bat is the Windows one, where some cmd.exe
# constructs need CRLF. Nothing enforced this before - the files happened to
# be stored correctly, and any contributor with a different core.autocrlf
# could have flipped either one.
* text=auto

*.sh text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.mp4 binary
